{
  "id": 21,
  "name": "spread_inverse_regret",
  "intent": "Invert the parent's spread-reliability gate to amplify regret when spread is low (uniform-like regimes where small regret differences are statistically reliable positional signals rather than noise). This targets uniform instances, where the parent suppressed regret too aggressively and lost central-access signal. Tighten the closing-leg return_distance ramp to (0.15 + 0.5p + 0.2p^2) for steeper late-tour emphasis addressing the residual tail gap. Add a small progress-gated cluster_density term (0.04*(1-p)) so early construction favors dense-remaining candidates, leveraging this feature before regret dominates. All weights bounded; ranking changes concentrate in low-spread regimes where the parent over-suppressed.",
  "tags": [
    "regret",
    "nonlinear"
  ],
  "code": "def priority(f):\n    p = f['progress']\n    s = f['spread']\n    rw = 0.15 + 0.5*p + 0.2*p*p\n    inv_s = 0.4/(0.4 + s + 1e-9)\n    rgw = (0.1 + 0.15*p) * (0.3 + 0.7*inv_s)\n    return -f['distance'] + rw*f['return_distance'] + rgw*f['regret'] + 0.08*f['nearest_remaining'] + 0.04*(1 - p)*f['cluster_density']",
  "source": "live_llm",
